<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4024.12">
  <DUT Name="E_VICI_EPS_PORT_STATUS" Id="{0243ee2e-9542-41eb-bd95-e56cebb740a9}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    E_VICI_EPS_PORT_STATUS - state of one port of a multi-port Vici selector
    valve, as seen by the equipment protection system (EPS).

    PURPOSE
        Says what one port of a 4-port or 12-port Vici valve is doing right now:
        whether the valve is routed to it (ACTIVE), whether it is free to be
        selected (UNLOCKED), or whether the EPS interlock flags of the port block
        it (LOCKED). Every port of the valve carries one of these values in the
        ePortStatus member of its E_VICI_PORT_EPS structure.

    USAGE
        Written once per PLC cycle by FB_VICI_EPS_LOGIC from the EPS flag word of
        every port (DUT_EPS: bEPS_OK is TRUE only while every bit of nFlags is
        TRUE):
            - every port is first set to UNLOCKED or LOCKED from its bEPS_OK;
            - the requested port is then set to ACTIVE when its bEPS_OK is TRUE
              or the temporary OVRD_MODE override is on, so on that port ACTIVE
              replaces the value its EPS flags alone would give.
        Read back by FB_VICI_EPS_LOGIC (the LOCKED comparison that raises
        bExternalLock) and published to EPICS by the ePortStatus pytmc pragma of
        E_VICI_PORT_EPS as the integer 0 / 1 / 2. Do not renumber the members:
        those numbers are the EPICS encoding and the value operators see.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Give the port state a named type instead of a bare INT, so that the
          logic, the tests and the EPICS consumers agree on what 0 / 1 / 2 mean.
        - Keep the two independent facts apart: ACTIVE says where the valve is
          routed, LOCKED says whether the EPS permits that port at all.

    PRECONDITIONS
        - A port can read ACTIVE while its own EPS flags are not OK: the ACTIVE
          assignment runs after the per-port EPS evaluation and the override path
          does not test bEPS_OK. Callers that need "routed and permitted" must
          test ACTIVE together with the port's DUT_EPS.bEPS_OK.
        - When the requested port is not permitted and no override is on, no
          port carries ACTIVE at all; FB_VICI_EPS_LOGIC then keeps the valve at
          the previous port, whose status is UNLOCKED or LOCKED.
        - The type is declared {attribute 'qualified_only'} and
          {attribute 'strict'}, so the members must always be written as
          E_VICI_EPS_PORT_STATUS.<member> and an unknown member is a compile
          error.

    UNITS
        None - a state, not a measurement. The 0 / 1 / 2 values exist only to
        give the ePortStatus EPICS record a stable integer.

    HISTORY
        2026-05-19 J. Zamudio - enum added as ENUM_PORT_STATUS with the Vici
            4-port valve EPS function block (06669bb); no member documented.
        2026-07-07 J. Zamudio - pre-commit style pass (01bbcff), contents
            unchanged.
        2026-07-17 J. Zamudio - renamed to E_VICI_EPS_PORT_STATUS and made
            qualified_only/strict in the generic FB_ViciValveEPS refactor
            (2810241); no member documented.
        2026-11-27 Scirix Agent - added this header and one comment per member
            (audit finding 1154); no member, value or pragma changed.
*)
{attribute 'qualified_only'}
{attribute 'strict'}
TYPE E_VICI_EPS_PORT_STATUS :
(
    // Port the valve is routed to. FB_VICI_EPS_LOGIC flags the requested port
    // (iNewPortPos) with it, replacing the UNLOCKED or LOCKED value that port's
    // own EPS flags would give, and only while that port's EPS flags are all
    // TRUE (DUT_EPS.bEPS_OK) or the temporary OVRD_MODE override is on. It is
    // the target port, so it is also the port the valve sits on from the next
    // scan on. No unit; EPICS value 0.
    ACTIVE := 0,

    // Port the valve may be routed to. All bits of the port's EPS flag word are
    // TRUE (DUT_EPS.bEPS_OK), so the equipment protection system permits it.
    // Every port that is not flagged ACTIVE on this scan carries UNLOCKED or
    // LOCKED, including the port the valve is currently sitting on, so UNLOCKED
    // alone does not mean the valve is there. No unit; EPICS value 1.
    UNLOCKED := 1,

    // Port the valve must not be routed to. At least one bit of the port's EPS
    // flag word is FALSE (DUT_EPS.bEPS_OK = FALSE), so the equipment protection
    // system blocks it and only the temporary OVRD_MODE override can still
    // select it. When the requested port is also the current one and LOCKED
    // without override, FB_VICI_EPS_LOGIC raises bExternalLock. No unit; EPICS
    // value 2.
    LOCKED := 2
);
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>